# Airbnb Slider — a price slider ($0..$4500) driving a rolling odometer: each
# digit is a column of 0-9 springing on translateY, leading zeros fade out and
# the "$" sign slides as the digit count changes (1 -> 4 digits).
# What this test covers: drag to the max (clamped at $4500) and past it, back to
# $0 and past the start (clamp, no negative price), a slow scrub through every
# digit-count boundary (9->10, 99->100, 999->1000), fast back-and-forth flicks
# that interrupt the digit springs, re-grabbing the thumb from a non-zero value,
# and taps on the track (no jump expected: only the thumb is draggable).
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/airbnb-slider"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 45000
# Warm-up touch on the status bar: the first touch of a test can be lost while
# the XCTest runner attaches.
press 330 20
wait 500
wait "text" "$" 10000
wait 1000
# Thumb starts at x=45 (track 45..357, y=480). Drag to the end and beyond.
gesture pan 45 480 340 0 800
wait 1000
gesture pan 352 480 45 0 500
wait 1000
# All the way back past the start.
gesture pan 357 480 -350 0 600
wait 1000
# Slow scrub from $0 across the 1/2/3/4-digit boundaries.
gesture pan 45 480 5 0 800
wait 600
gesture pan 50 480 10 0 800
wait 600
gesture pan 60 480 40 0 1200
wait 600
gesture pan 100 480 200 0 3000
wait 1000
# Fast flicks back and forth (springs interrupted mid-roll).
gesture pan 300 480 -200 0 150
gesture pan 100 480 200 0 150
gesture pan 300 480 -150 0 150
wait 1200
# Taps on the empty track away from the thumb.
press 330 480
wait 500
press 60 480
wait 800
# Re-grab the thumb (now at x~150) and drag it back past the start ($0).
gesture pan 150 480 -120 0 500
wait 1000
wait "text" "$" 3000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 15000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
